  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 203 of the laws of 1957 authorizing the town of\nBallston, Saratoga county, to establish a public library for that part of the\ntown located outside of the incorporated village of Ballston Spa, in relation\nto providing for the election of trustees and voter approval of the tax levy\nof such library district; and to amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993,\namending the public authorities law relating to the construction and financing\nof facilities for certain public libraries, in relation to including the\nBallston Community Public Library",
    "basePrintNo": "S6669",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6669-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Chap 203 of 1957; amd §5, Chap 672 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Saratoga County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6669\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 203 of the laws of 1957 authorizing the town of\nBallston, Saratoga county, to establish a public library for that part\nof the town located outside of the incorporated village of Ballston Spa,\nin relation to providing for the election of trustees and voter approval\nof the tax levy of such library district; and to amend chapter 672 of\nthe laws of 1993, amending the public authorities law relating to the\nconstruction and financing of facilities for certain public libraries,\nin relation to including the Ballston Community Public Library\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRelates to the administration and funding of the town of Ballston Commu-\nnity Public Library and the creation of a public library district\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nChapter 203 of the laws of 1957 authorizing the town of Ballston, Sara-\ntoga County, to establish a public library for that part of the town\nlocated outside of the incorporated village of Ballston Spa, is amended\nto read as follows:\n\n§ 1. Establishes provisions and precedent for the creation of a public\nlibrary district.\n\n§ 2. Lays out the parameters related to the approval of a budget, public\nhearings and a ballot proposal for the public to approve formation of\nthe aforementioned district, and annual elections thereafter to estab-\nlish a Board of Trustees along with annual budgets.\n\n§ 3. Relates to the Organization and structure of the district.\n\n§ 4. Covers all parameters of the financial structure of the district\nand funding mechanism.\n\n§ 5. Charter, bylaws and transfer. The current charter of the Ballston\nCommunity Public Library is consistent with this legislation. The\ninitial elected trustees shall, within thirty days from the date of\napproval of the library budget and new trustees by the voters of the\ndistrict, adopt revised bylaws consistent with this legislation. The\nlibrary, which has operated as a special district library since 1957,\nshall continue to operate, uninterrupted, regardless of whether the\nbudget and election of trustees goes into effect. The town may transfer\ntitle to any existing or future real property to the library, or grant a\n99-year lease for an agreed upon rental rate, with optional renewal and\nright of first refusal in the event of transfer, for the purposes of\noperating a library or branch of the library within the district.\n\n§ 6. Ad valorem levy. The several lots and parcels of land within the\narea of such public library district are hereby determined to be bene-\nfited by the library facilities and devices existing as of the effective\ndate of this act and the town of Ballston is hereby authorized to\nassess, levy and collect the necessary expenses of operation, mainte-\nnance and repair of such facilities and services and such capital\nimprovements, including debt service on bonds, notes or other evidences\nof indebtedness issued for the purpose of the Ballston Community Public\nLibrary as may be hereafter authorized pursuant to the provisions of\nthis act from such lots and parcels of land within the library district,\noutside of the limits of the village of Ballston Spa, in the same manner\nand at the same time as other town charges.\n\n§ 7. Education law. Except as otherwise provided by this act, the\nprovisions of the education law relating to public libraries shall be\napplicable to the Ballston Community Public Library operating as estab-\nlished by this act.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Ballston Community Public Library seeks a charter update to bring\nthem in line with how Special District Libraries operate in the year\n2023. Their original charter is from 1957. After coordinating with the\nTown, both entities proposed legislation that they are confident will\ngarner public support. Each of these respective Boards voted to proceed\nwith this measure.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\n2 of this act shall take effect sixty days after the initial budget\nproposed in section two of chapter 203 of the laws of 1957 authorizing\nthe town of Ballston, Saratoga county, to establish a public library for\nthat part of the town located outside of the incorporated village of\nBallston Spa, as amended by section one of this act, is approved by a\nvote of the majority of the qualified voters voting in an election as\nprovided in such chapter.\n",
